/*
The statement provided is incomplete in this prompt, but the core task is:

Given n candidate positions for unit cubes in 3D, choose exactly k of them so that the chosen cubes form
one connected polycube (face-connectivity), and the total surface area is minimal.

For a set of chosen cubes:
surface = 6*k - 2*(number of face-adjacent chosen pairs)

So minimizing surface is equivalent to maximizing the number of face-adjacent pairs among the chosen k cubes,
under the constraint that the chosen cubes are connected.

We build the graph on the given positions where edges connect positions at Manhattan distance 1.
Then we need a connected induced-by-vertices subset of size k maximizing internal edges.

This is NP-hard in general, but the intended task in classical contest settings with such wording typically
has small n (e.g. n <= 20..25), allowing DP over subsets. We implement exact subset DP:

- Build adjacency bitmasks.
- For every subset S, compute:
  * size
  * whether connected
  * number of internal graph edges
- Among connected subsets of size k, maximize internal edges.
- Answer = 6*k - 2*bestEdges.

Connectivity DP:
A subset S is connected iff removing one chosen "least significant" vertex r leaves T=S\{r} connected and
r has a neighbor in T, OR |S|=1.
This recurrence works because every connected graph has a non-articulation vertex, but using only the least
significant bit is not generally sufficient as a characterization. So instead we do a standard BFS/bit-DFS per subset.
This is acceptable for small n.

Internal edges:
For subset S, edges(S) = sum over v in S of popcount(adj[v] & S) / 2.

This solution is exact for small n.

Input format assumed:
n k
x1 y1 z1
...
xn yn zn

Output:
minimal surface area

If k=0, output 0.
*/
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);
        int n;
        try {
            n = fs.nextInt();
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return;
        }
        int k = fs.nextInt();

        long[] x = new long[n];
        long[] y = new long[n];
        long[] z = new long[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            x[i] = fs.nextLong();
            y[i] = fs.nextLong();
            z[i] = fs.nextLong();
        }

        if (k == 0) {
            System.out.println(0);
            return;
        }
        if (k > n) {
            // Impossible under any reasonable interpretation; keep behavior safe.
            System.out.println(-1);
            return;
        }
        if (n > 25) {
            // Exact subset DP becomes infeasible; however the original problem constraints are expected small.
            // We still provide a safe guard.
            System.out.println(-1);
            return;
        }

        long[] adj = new long[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            long mask = 0L;
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                if (i == j) continue;
                long d = Math.abs(x[i] - x[j]) + Math.abs(y[i] - y[j]) + Math.abs(z[i] - z[j]);
                if (d == 1) mask |= 1L << j;
            }
            adj[i] = mask;
        }

        int total = 1 << n;
        int[] pop = new int[total];
        int[] edges = new int[total];
        boolean[] conn = new boolean[total];

        int best = -1;

        for (int s = 1; s < total; s++) {
            pop[s] = pop[s >>> 1] + (s & 1);

            if (pop[s] > k) continue;

            // compute internal edges incrementally by adding lsb vertex
            int lsb = s & -s;
            int v = Integer.numberOfTrailingZeros(lsb);
            int t = s ^ lsb;
            edges[s] = edges[t] + Long.bitCount(adj[v] & (long) t);

            if (pop[s] == 1) {
                conn[s] = true;
            } else {
                conn[s] = isConnected(s, adj, n);
            }

            if (pop[s] == k && conn[s]) {
                if (edges[s] > best) best = edges[s];
            }
        }

        if (best < 0) {
            System.out.println(-1);
            return;
        }

        int ans = 6 * k - 2 * best;
        System.out.println(ans);
    }

    static boolean isConnected(int s, long[] adj, int n) {
        int start = Integer.numberOfTrailingZeros(s);
        int seen = 0;
        int[] stack = new int[n];
        int top = 0;
        stack[top++] = start;
        seen |= 1 << start;

        while (top > 0) {
            int v = stack[--top];
            long nei = adj[v] & (long) s;
            while (nei != 0) {
                long bit = nei & -nei;
                int u = Long.numberOfTrailingZeros(bit);
                if ((seen & (1 << u)) == 0) {
                    seen |= 1 << u;
                    stack[top++] = u;
                }
                nei ^= bit;
            }
        }
        return seen == s;
    }

    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        long nextLong() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do {
                c = read();
                if (c == -1) throw new EOFException();
            } while (c <= ' ');

            int sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }

            long val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            return (int) nextLong();
        }
    }
}
